+- **Native** — I implement every task myself in this session, then one fresh reviewer checks the whole branch. Cheapest and fastest; no independent review until the end.
+
+For this plan I recommend **Native**, because the tasks have tight interdependencies (parser output feeds into generateReport, report structure feeds into reporters), so a single implementer can maintain consistency efficiently. The plan's design carries the complexity, so a mid-tier model can execute it reliably. Final review by a fresh reviewer catches any misses.
+
+Does the plan capture what you want?
